<p>NOTE: The Company decided to exit its commercial engine services business and this business was recorded as a discontinued operation as of December 31, 1995.  All financial statements were restated to reflect such classification. The $212.5 million charge taken in the fourth quarter of 1995 included a projection of future results for the discontinued operation through the estimated disposal date.</p>
<p>The $3.4 million extraordinary item resulted from the write-off of unamortized debt issuance costs associated with the Company's 1993 credit agreement which was refinanced in the third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>Company also recorded a non-recurring pretax charge of $33.2 million to revalue the aerospace fastener distribution business sold during the third quarter 1996.</p>
